course: dictionary
lesson: 4604
title: Pausing before you act
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To hesitate means to stop or pause before you do or say something, because you are unsure, nervous or worried. Your brain is stuck for a moment, not sure which way to go. «Ethan in Chicago hears three instructions at once; the brain can only follow one at a time, it hesitates for a split second, and the chance is gone.» The pause is short, but it is enough to lose the ball.
explain: Hesitate can also mean the opposite of pausing. When someone says «Don't hesitate to ask», they mean feel free to ask now, straight away. Look at the words around it: a teacher offering help is not asking you to wait and think about it for a long time.
explain: Hesitate has forms you can spot in a sentence: hesitate, hesitates, hesitated and hesitating. «Without hesitating» means straight away, with no pause at all. Ask yourself: is the person pausing because they are unsure, or are they being invited to act at once?
fact: To hesitate means to pause before doing or saying something.
fact: You hesitate when you are unsure, nervous or worried.
fact: «Don't hesitate to» means feel free to do it at once.
fact: «Without hesitating» means straight away, with no pause.
fact: Hesitate is a verb: hesitate, hesitates, hesitated, hesitating.
exercise: «...it hesitates for a split second, and the chance is gone.» What does hesitates mean here? | Forgets everything for ever | Runs very fast | *Pauses because it cannot decide what to do | Shouts loudly
exercise: Mum says, «Don't hesitate to ask if you need help.» What does she mean? | Never ask anything | *Feel free to ask straight away | Wait a long time before you ask
exercise: Which word shows hesitate in the past tense? | hesitate | *hesitated | hesitates | hesitating
test: Yesterday Sam ___ before he answered the tricky question. | hesitate | *hesitated | hesitating
test: What does «without hesitating» mean in «She jumped in without hesitating»? | After a long wait | While she was asleep | *Straight away, with no pause | In a slow, careful way
exam: Which sentence shows someone who does not hesitate? | Ruby stood still, unsure, for a long time | Ruby looked away and hid behind the door | *Ruby grabbed the rope and climbed up at once | Ruby asked whether she should try, then waited
